## Direct Recommendation

The workspace's display `name` never reaches the tab because it is not carried on the **app object**. `workspaces.open()` forwards the workspace object into params, but the tab's `name` resolution only ever sees the generic app title (`def.title`). Fix: name the app after the workspace in `navigate.js`, and let `Tab.vue` fall back to the app's `name` (never touching the chat/board precedence).

## Root Cause

Tracing `openApp('workspace', { workspace })`:

```js
// navigate.js → openApp()
name: payload.name || def.title   // ← payload.name is never set for a workspace
```

`workspaces.open()` computes `const name = workspace.name || …` but **only uses it in the chat branch**. In the normal branch it passes just `{ workspace }`, so the app is named `def.title` ("Workspace"). In `Tab.vue`:

```js
tabName() {
  return this.chat?.name ||          // ok for chats
    this.boardName ||                // ok for boards
    this.workspace?.name ||          // params snapshot — often missing the name
    this.workspace?.title ||
    this.app?.title ||               // ← generic "Workspace" leaks through here
    this.params?.params?.tabName
}
```

`this.app?.name` (the natural display name for a panel) is **never consulted**, so the workspace `name` has no path to the label.

## Specifications

| Dimension | Decision |
|---|---|
| **Source of truth** | The workspace object's `name` → lifted onto the app/panel `name` |
| **Fallback order** | `chat.name` → `boardName` → `workspace.name` → `workspace.title` → **`app.name`** → `app.title` → `params.tabName` |
| **Isolation** | Chat panels are resolved first (unchanged); boards keep precedence (unchanged); only workspace payloads gain a name |
| **Data flow** | `workspaces.open()` → `openApp('workspace', { workspace, name })` → `showApp({ name })` → `Tab` reads `app.name` |

## Code Changes

### 1. `src/router/navigate.js` — forward the resolved name (workspace-only)

In `workspaces.open()`, the computed `name` was only forwarded in the chat branch. Forward it in the normal branch too, so the panel/app is labelled with the workspace `name`:

```js router/navigate.js
        // Forward the whole workspace under the `workspace` key (same
        // convention as `chat`) so name/path reach the panel params, and pass
        // the resolved name so the panel is labelled with the workspace `name`
        // (the tab falls back to the app `name` when the params carry none).
        openApp('workspace', { workspace, name })
```

> Only the `workspaces.open` call site changes — `chats.open`, `chats.openWithWorkspace`, `meets.*` and the `workspaces.list()` opener are untouched.

### 2. `src/components/desktop/Tab.vue` — consult the app `name`

```vue src/components/desktop/Tab.vue
<script setup>
import AppIcon from '../apps/AppIcon.vue'
</script>
<template>
  <div
    class="codx-tab flex gap-1 items-center justify-between px-1 py-0.5 border rounded-xl w-40 text-md"
    :draggable="!!chat"
    :class="{ 'cursor-grab active:cursor-grabbing': !!chat }"
    @dragstart="onDragStart"
  >
    <div class="w-4/5 flex gap-1 items-center truncate overflow-hidden">
      <!-- Pass loading state to AppIcon so it shows the ring inside the icon area -->
      <AppIcon :app="app || workspace" :loading="isUpdating" />
      <div class="grow truncate overflow-hidden">{{ tabName }}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="click hover:text-warning shrink-0 mr-2" @click="onClose">
      <i class="fa-solid fa-xmark fa-sm"></i>
    </div>
  </div>
</template>
<script>

export default {
  props: ['params'],
  data() {
    return {
      project: null,
    }
  },
  async created() {
    this.project = this.$projects.allProjectsById[this.projectId]
  },
  computed: {
    chat() {
      const chatId = this.params?.params?.chat?.id
      return this.$storex.chats.chats[chatId]
    },
    // Read the app from the live store (not the static panel snapshot) so
    // runtime app-info updates — such as the active board name — are reflected
    // in the tab without recreating the panel.
    app() {
      const app = this.params?.params?.app
      return (app?.tabId && this.$storex.ui.openApps[app.tabId]) || app
    },
    // Workspace panels carry the raw workspace (name, path, …) in params under
    // the `workspace` key; fall back to the legacy `app` slot for old payloads.
    workspace() {
      return this.params?.params?.workspace || this.app
    },
    // Name of the board the panel is currently showing. The board view
    // publishes it into the app params when the active board changes.
    boardName() {
      return this.app?.params?.boardName || null
    },
    tabName() {
      // Precedence matters: chats and boards keep their name first, then the
      // workspace object, then the app name/title. Adding `app?.name` lets a
      // workspace opened with a name-only payload (no `workspace` in params)
      // still surface the workspace `name` instead of the generic title.
      return this.chat?.name ||
        this.boardName ||
        this.workspace?.name ||
        this.workspace?.title ||
        this.app?.name ||
        this.app?.title ||
        this.params?.params?.tabName
    },
    api() {
      return this.params.api
    },
    containerApi() {
      return this.params.containerApi
    },
    panel() {
      return this.api.panel
    },
    projectId() {
      return this.params?.params?.project_id
    },
    isUpdating() {
      return this.$storex.chats.isChatUpdating(this.chat?.id)
    }
  },
  methods: {
    onDragStart(event) {
      // Only register a sprint task id when the tab is backed by a chat
      if (!this.chat) return
      event.dataTransfer.setData('sprintTaskId', this.chat.id)
      event.dataTransfer.effectAllowed = 'move'
    },
    onClose() {
      this.containerApi.removePanel(this.panel)
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

## Anti-Patterns Avoided

- ❌ Reading the name from `this.params.params.name` blindly — that slot is used by other payload shapes and would leak a wrong label into chats/boards.
- ❌ Reordering the precedence so `app.name` beats `workspace.name`/`chat.name` — that would show the generic app title on a chat-workspace panel.
- ❌ Setting the workspace name inside `Tab` — the name belongs on the app/panel so it survives layout persistence and reloads.

## Accessibility Checklist

- [x] No behavior change for keyboard/focus; only the visible label text changes.
- [x] Long workspace names remain truncated (`truncate overflow-hidden`) — no layout break, no loss of the tooltip-free affordance.
- [x] The label is the only difference; icon/close affordances untouched.

## Implementation Steps

1. In `src/router/navigate.js` → `workspaces.open()`, change `openApp('workspace', { workspace })` to `openApp('workspace', { workspace, name })`.
2. In `src/components/desktop/Tab.vue` → `tabName()`, insert `this.app?.name ||` between `this.workspace?.title` and `this.app?.title`.
3. Verify: open a workspace from the Workspaces list → tab shows the workspace `name`; open a chat and a board → labels unchanged (chat name / board name still win).

